# AI Compliance Inspector — frontend

This repo is **frontend only**. Do not implement OCR, image processing, translation, extraction, JSON generation, compliance/rule engines, sanction decisions, evidence generation, RAG, official-source fetching, MongoDB, auth/JWT/session internals, or backend report generation.

## Architecture

- `pages/` and `components/` render UI from props/state. They do not own business rules or HTTP.
- `services/` is the only place for API clients. UI talks to services, never `fetch` in components.
- `types/` holds frontend/API models. `hooks/` holds reusable client behavior. `mocks/` holds fixtures.
- Replace mocks with real APIs later without rewriting screens. Do not add fake network calls until that batch.

## Design

Use semantic tokens (`bg`, `surface`, `ink`, `muted`, `border`, `brand`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `info`). Navy/slate foundation, blue accent, calm enterprise workstation. No cyberpunk, heavy gradients, glassmorphism, or extra animation.

Reuse `Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Badge`, `LoadingState`, and layout (`AppShell`, `Sidebar`, `Navbar`, `PageHeader`). Do not duplicate primitives.

## Scope

Build only the requested batch. Route placeholders stay placeholders until their feature batch. Do not install dependencies unless clearly needed now.

## Efficiency

Do not regenerate scaffolding, re-explain architecture, or expand scope. Prefer small diffs. After UI work: typecheck/build and fix issues you introduced.
